---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Link } from "../components/Link";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Swarnim Walavalkar — Work"
  description="Things I've done in the past"
>
  <main class="prose">
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-12">
      <!-- Devfolio -->
      <section class="group">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
          <h3
            class="!font-serif !text-2xl !font-normal !tracking-tight !text-neutral-50"
          >
            <a
              href="https://devfolio.co/"
              target="_blank"
              class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-white"
              >Devfolio</a
            >
          </h3>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span
              class="rounded-full border border-emerald-800/50 bg-emerald-900/40 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-emerald-300"
              >Current</span
            >
            <time class="text-sm text-neutral-500">Since 2023</time>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4 font-serif text-xl italic leading-snug text-neutral-200">
          Building software that helps builders turn projects into
          opportunities.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-neutral-400">
          <p>
            I care about helping strong builders get seen for the quality of
            their work. At Devfolio, that has meant building across the full
            arc: tools that help people start, systems that help them get useful
            feedback on what they made, and products that help the right grant
            programs, fellowships, collaborators, and hiring teams find them.
          </p>
          <p>
            A lot of that work has involved evaluation, discovery, and more
            programmatic interfaces into the platform. Right now, AI happens to
            be the right technology for some of those problems, especially when
            the goal is to understand work better, find overlooked talent, and
            make access easier for both people and agents.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="relative mt-10">
          <div
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="pointer-events-none absolute bottom-2 left-0 top-2 w-px bg-gradient-to-b from-neutral-800/0 via-neutral-800 to-neutral-800/0"
          >
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-12 pl-7">
            <!-- i · AI products -->
            <article class="relative">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="absolute -left-[31px] top-[7px] block h-[7px] w-[7px] rotate-45 border border-neutral-700 bg-stone-950 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:border-neutral-500"
              ></span>
              <p
                class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-neutral-500"
              >
                <span class="text-neutral-600">i</span>
                <span class="mx-2 text-neutral-700">·</span>
                <span class="text-neutral-300">AI products</span>
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
                I led a lot of Devfolio's work here. The aim was simple: build
                better tools for understanding builder work, evaluating it
                fairly, and helping the right people notice it.
              </p>
              <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-400">
                <li>
                  Built AI-assisted project assessment systems that generate
                  structured reports on hackathon projects. They summarize what
                  a project does, what stands out, how original it is, what
                  similar work exists, and where it fits in a broader technical
                  landscape.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Built application review systems that give organizers better
                  rubric-based signals and make large-scale review less noisy
                  and more tractable.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Built agentic judging systems that inspect submitted repos
                  inside isolated sandboxes, run tools against real codebases,
                  and produce evaluation reports with evidence and code
                  references.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <!-- ii · Scout -->
            <article class="relative">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="absolute -left-[31px] top-[7px] block h-[7px] w-[7px] rotate-45 border border-neutral-700 bg-stone-950 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:border-neutral-500"
              ></span>
              <p
                class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-neutral-500"
              >
                <span class="text-neutral-600">ii</span>
                <span class="mx-2 text-neutral-700">·</span>
                <span class="text-neutral-300">Scout</span>
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
                Scout is probably the clearest expression of this direction so
                far. It is a talent search product built to surface underrated
                but truly exceptional builders by reading across their
                proof-of-work: projects, hackathon history, open source
                activity, technical writing, onchain credentials, and other
                public artifacts of real work.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
                The vision is to build a much better map of technical talent
                than a résumé or keyword search can offer. Instead of flattening
                people into a single score, Scout tries to capture the many ways
                good builders show up: depth, range, taste, and sustained
                curiosity across domains.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
                In the best case, it helps surface people who might otherwise be
                missed: strong but under-recognized builders whose public work
                already shows that they are unusually capable.
              </p>
            </article>

            <!-- iii · The Synthesis -->
            <article class="relative">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="absolute -left-[31px] top-[7px] block h-[7px] w-[7px] rotate-45 border border-neutral-700 bg-stone-950 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:border-neutral-500"
              ></span>
              <p
                class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-neutral-500"
              >
                <span class="text-neutral-600">iii</span>
                <span class="mx-2 text-neutral-700">·</span>
                <span class="text-neutral-300">The Synthesis</span>
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
                I built <a
                  href="https://synthesis.md/"
                  target="_blank"
                  class="underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-3 transition-colors duration-200 hover:decoration-neutral-400"
                  >The Synthesis</a
                > platform end to end, an AI agents-only hackathon we hosted
                with friends from the Ethereum ecosystem. It was a chance to
                take the question seriously: what does software look like when
                agents are primary users, not an afterthought?
              </p>
              <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-400">
                <li>
                  Built the entire agent-native platform for registration,
                  project submission, bounties, and prize disbursement.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Designed the human-agent collaboration model and the broader
                  product shape of the system.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Shipped AustinXBT, a voice-first AI judging / mentorship
                  interface, in under 48 hours during the event.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <!-- iv · Voice agents -->
            <article class="relative">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="absolute -left-[31px] top-[7px] block h-[7px] w-[7px] rotate-45 border border-neutral-700 bg-stone-950 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:border-neutral-500"
              ></span>
              <p
                class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-neutral-500"
              >
                <span class="text-neutral-600">iv</span>
                <span class="mx-2 text-neutral-700">·</span>
                <span class="text-neutral-300"
                  >Hackathon mentorship AI voice agents</span
                >
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
                I also built AI voice agents inspired by <a
                  href="https://www.jessepollak.com/"
                  target="_blank"
                  class="underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-3 transition-colors duration-200 hover:decoration-neutral-400"
                  >Jesse Pollak</a
                > and <a
                  href="https://x.com/austingriffith"
                  target="_blank"
                  class="underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-3 transition-colors duration-200 hover:decoration-neutral-400"
                  >Austin Griffith</a
                >. Both are prominent builder-facing mentors, and both were keen
                on the idea. The goal was to make mentorship and judging more
                accessible, more personal, and easier to scale.
              </p>
              <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-400">
                <li>
                  Started with JesseGPT, a voice-first mentor agent in the
                  likeness of Jesse Pollak.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Later reused and extended that work to ship AustinXBT for The
                  Synthesis.
                </li>
                <li>
                  These projects doubled as experiments in making mentor / judge
                  personas customizable, reusable, and deployable quickly.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <!-- v · Programmatic & composable -->
            <article class="relative">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="absolute -left-[31px] top-[7px] block h-[7px] w-[7px] rotate-45 border border-neutral-700 bg-stone-950 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:border-neutral-500"
              ></span>
              <p
                class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-neutral-500"
              >
                <span class="text-neutral-600">v</span>
                <span class="mx-2 text-neutral-700">·</span>
                <span class="text-neutral-300"
                  >A more programmatic, composable platform</span
                >
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
                A parallel thread in my work has been making Devfolio easier to
                interact with as a system through clear APIs, simple primitives,
                and interfaces that other software can compose.
              </p>
              <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-400">
                <li>
                  Built Devfolio's MCP server, allowing AI agents to fetch
                  hackathons, explore prizes, suggest relevant tracks, and help
                  with project submissions.
                </li>
                <li>
                  More broadly, I've cared about making the core platform more
                  programmatic and composable because better shaped primitives
                  make Devfolio easier to build on and naturally more legible to
                  agents.
                </li>
                <li>
                  That thread became even clearer while working on The
                  Synthesis.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <!-- vi · Other -->
            <article class="relative">
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="absolute -left-[31px] top-[7px] block h-[7px] w-[7px] rotate-45 border border-neutral-700 bg-stone-950 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:border-neutral-500"
              ></span>
              <p
                class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-neutral-500"
              >
                <span class="text-neutral-600">vi</span>
                <span class="mx-2 text-neutral-700">·</span>
                <span class="text-neutral-300">Other things I've shipped</span>
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
                Beyond the work above, I've also worked on a range of
                builder-facing platform features and primitives.
              </p>
              <ul
                class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-6 gap-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-400 sm:grid-cols-2"
              >
                <li>
                  <Link
                    target="_blank"
                    href="https://devfolio.co/blog/onchain-credentials-helping-you-put-your-proof-of-work-on-the-blockchain/"
                    class="underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-3 transition-colors duration-200 hover:decoration-neutral-400"
                  >
                    Onchain credentials
                  </Link>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <Link
                    target="_blank"
                    href="https://attest.sh/"
                    class="underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-3 transition-colors duration-200 hover:decoration-neutral-400"
                  >
                    EAS attestations
                  </Link>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <Link
                    target="_blank"
                    href="https://devfolio.co/blog/introooducing-quadratic-voting-on-devfolio/"
                    class="underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-3 transition-colors duration-200 hover:decoration-neutral-400"
                  >
                    Quadratic voting
                  </Link>
                </li>
                <li>
                  Internal tooling &amp; workflow improvements for running large
                  technical programs
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <details class="past-lives group/past mt-4">
        <summary
          class="cursor-pointer select-none list-none rounded-sm py-2 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"
        >
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-neutral-800 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/past:to-neutral-700"
            ></span>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-neutral-400 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/past:text-neutral-200"
                >Past Lives</span
              >
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tabular-nums tracking-[0.22em] text-neutral-600 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/past:text-neutral-500"
                >· 04</span
              >
              <span
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="relative ml-1 inline-flex h-3 w-3 items-center justify-center text-neutral-500 transition-all duration-300 group-open/past:rotate-45 group-open/past:text-neutral-300 group-hover/past:text-neutral-300"
              >
                <span
                  class="absolute inset-x-0 top-1/2 h-px -translate-y-1/2 bg-current"
                ></span>
                <span
                  class="absolute inset-y-0 left-1/2 w-px -translate-x-1/2 bg-current"
                ></span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-l from-transparent to-neutral-800 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover/past:to-neutral-700"
            ></span>
          </div>
        </summary>

        <div class="mt-12 space-y-12">
          <!-- Now&Me -->
          <section>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-100">
                <a
                  href="https://nowandme.com/"
                  target="_blank"
                  class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-white"
                  >Now&Me</a
                >
              </h3>
              <time class="text-sm tabular-nums text-neutral-500"
                >2022 — 2023</time
              >
            </div>

            <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-400">
              A peer-to-peer mental health platform
            </p>

            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-400">
              <li>Learned a ton about building community/social apps</li>
              <li>
                Learned a ton about product analytics + user behavior analysis
              </li>
              <li>Learned a ton about building scalable Kubernetes infra</li>
              <li>Built robust internal tools for UGC moderation</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <div class="border-t border-neutral-800/60"></div>

          <!-- COVID Army -->
          <section>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-100">
                <a
                  href="https://github.com/covidarmy/"
                  target="_blank"
                  class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-white"
                  >COVID Army</a
                >
              </h3>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span
                  class="rounded-full border border-sky-800/40 bg-sky-900/30 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-sky-300"
                  >Public Good</span
                >
                <time class="text-sm tabular-nums text-neutral-500">2021</time>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-400">
              A platform to find lifesaving COVID related resources across 1200
              indian cities at the height of the COVID 19 pandemic
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
              <a
                target="_blank"
                href="https://github.com/covidarmy"
                class="underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-3 transition-colors duration-200 hover:decoration-neutral-400"
                >github.com/covidarmy</a
              >
            </p>
          </section>

          <div class="border-t border-neutral-800/60"></div>

          <!-- Cato TV -->
          <section>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-100">
                <a
                  href="https://github.com/catoverse/"
                  target="_blank"
                  class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-white"
                  >Cato TV</a
                >
              </h3>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span
                  class="rounded-full border border-indigo-800/40 bg-indigo-900/30 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-indigo-300"
                  >Open Source</span
                >
                <time class="text-sm tabular-nums text-neutral-500"
                  >2021 — 2022</time
                >
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-400">
              An ambitious education video platform, that aimed to curate the
              best knowledge on the internet.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-neutral-400">
              This was my first time working in a team, Learned a ton; about
              engineering, product and people.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-neutral-400">
              Built cool shit with incredible people and fostered some of my
              closest friendships
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-neutral-400">
              We bit off more than we could chew at the time, the product
              unfortunately never came to fruition.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">
              <a
                target="_blank"
                href="https://github.com/catoverse"
                class="underline decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-3 transition-colors duration-200 hover:decoration-neutral-400"
                >github.com/catoverse</a
              >
            </p>
          </section>

          <div class="border-t border-neutral-800/60"></div>

          <!-- Navgurukul Labs -->
          <section>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-100">
                Navgurukul Labs
              </h3>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span
                  class="rounded-full border border-sky-800/40 bg-sky-900/30 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-sky-300"
                  >Public Good</span
                >
                <time class="text-sm tabular-nums text-neutral-500"
                  >Early 2022</time
                >
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-400">
              Got in touch with Navgurukul through friends at Cato, Cato was
              briefly a part of Navgurukul Labs before we ultimately decided to
              move on...
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-neutral-400">
              Briefly volunteered to help with engineering and some misc product
              management for various initiatives within the org.
            </p>

            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-400">
              <li>
                Led the Cato TV engineering team for a while (poorly). I was
                clueless. Learned a ton
              </li>
              <li>Learned to be a product-focused engineer</li>
              <li>Started to build a product intuition</li>
              <li>
                Learned the importance of talking to users, and not building in
                a void
              </li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .past-lives > summary {
    outline: none;
  }

  .past-lives > summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 1px solid rgb(82 82 82);
    outline-offset: 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .past-lives::details-content {
    block-size: 0;
    overflow: clip;
    opacity: 0;
    transition:
      block-size 360ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      opacity 240ms ease,
      content-visibility 360ms allow-discrete;
  }

  .past-lives[open]::details-content {
    block-size: auto;
    opacity: 1;
  }

  @supports (interpolate-size: allow-keywords) {
    .past-lives {
      interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
    }
  }
</style>
